    {'para': '**430. Verbs. Reduplicating Class.** This class forms the present-stem by prefixing a reduplication to the root.∗'},
    {'para': '**431.** The rules governing the reduplication are as follows:'},
    {'para': '1. The consonant of the reduplicating syllable is in general the first consonant of the root; thus, ⟨dā⟩, ⟨dadā⟩. But, (*a*) a non-aspirate is substituted for an aspirate; and (*b*) a palatal for a guttural'},
    {'para': 'or ⟨h⟩; thus, ⟨dhā⟩, ⟨dadhā⟩; ⟨khid⟩, ⟨cikhid⟩; ⟨hrī⟩, ⟨jihrī⟩; (*c*) if the root begin with a sibilant followed by a non-nasal mute, the latter is repeated (with observance of *a*), not the sibilant; thus, ⟨sthā⟩, ⟨tasthā⟩.'},
    {'para': '2. A long vowel is shortened in the reduplicating syllable; and ⟨ṛ⟩ is replaced by ⟨i⟩; thus, ⟨dadā⟩ and ⟨dadhā⟩ above; ⟨bhī⟩, ⟨bibhī⟩; ⟨bhṛ⟩, ⟨bibhṛ⟩.'},
    {'para': '**432.** The present-stem gunates the root-vowel in the strong forms; thus, ⟨bibhī⟩, strong ⟨bibhe⟩; ⟨bibhṛ⟩, strong ⟨bibhar⟩.'},
